  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" para="true">Valde Venerabili Viro,</l>
    <l n="2" type="heading" level="1">HERMANNO</l>
    <l n="3" type="heading" level="1">WITSIO Academicas in Symbolum Oecumenicum</l>
    <l n="4" type="heading" level="1">Exercitationes edenti,</l>
    <l n="5" type="heading" level="1">Doctori &amp; Praeceptori, optimo,</l>
    <l n="6" type="heading" level="1">incomparabili, SCAZON.</l>
    <l n="7" para="true">
      <i>AT quo Calore quove conciti motu</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Meritas Tibi speremus eloqui laudes</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Titulosque, Witsi? quo rapis Tui plenos</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Vi blandiore, quosve ducis in saltus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Succo fluentes atque coelico rore,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Quo terrae ocellus ille sacrosanctorum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Potor fluentorum, illa Terra Belgarum,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Coelestioris prima conda Doctrinae,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Nil divius nil purius bibit quidquam?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Jam diu diserta vidimus rudimenta</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Sacri laboris: quamque teste fers Coelo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Scientiaeque &amp; Conscientiae laudem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Miramur olim. Seu minacis Interpres</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Tonantis aerumnabile illud abs alto</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Quod quondam Amosides onus tulit Vates,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Diamque Litem atlamque saepius canssam,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Ter maximi optimique Numinis caussam,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Jussus redordiri, impiata vineta</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Putator ambis, sordidumque labruscas</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Pretium laborum traducesque silvestres</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>Sterilesque truncos atque degener colle</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>Recidis omni rejicisque sarmentum.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="29">
      <i>Seu inficeto, &amp; oris inverecundi,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="30">
      <i>Et obstinato calcitrare Livori,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="31">
      <i>Cordata quam facunda non minus scripta</i>
    </l>
    <l n="32">
      <i>Reponis, &amp; non absque tædio multo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="33">
      <i>Cuncta eloquutum ulciscERIS pie, menti</i>
    </l>
    <l n="34">
      <i>Bona intonatum devovendo, &amp; edurum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="35">
      <i>in Caput benignos colligendo carbones</i>
    </l>
    <l n="36">
      <i>Multum adstupenti. Quis modestior Paci</i>
    </l>
    <l n="37">
      <i>Silentium donare? fortior verba</i>
    </l>
    <l n="38">
      <i>Prœbere Vero? ne sibi furor pugnax</i>
    </l>
    <l n="39">
      <i>Insanientis aut Scientiæ turbo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="40" type="foot" para="true">
      <i>Doctrina</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Dedication poem in Latin with some illegible or doubtful letters; the line "Cuncta eloquutum ulciscERIS" and similar readings are uncertain. Lines marked as printed by the scan's typeface; a few words may be misread. Show-through and specks omitted.</notes>
</page>
